.TH "libnvmf_config_emit_write_file" 9 "libnvmf_config_emit_write_file" "November 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_config_emit_write_file \- Write the connections of one host to one file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_config_emit_write_file
.BI "(struct libnvmf_config_emitter *emitter "  ","
.BI "const char *file "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "emitter" 12
Configuration emitter.
.IP "file" 12
Destination file.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Writes the connections of \fIemitter\fP, with their host in a [Host]
section, to \fIfile\fP, which is replaced. Unlike
\fBlibnvmf_config_emit_install\fP, a connection with a host of its own
goes into \fIfile\fP too, so a caller can write a drop-in of its own: all
connections must have the same host. The file is validated by reading
it back, written atomically, and only readable by its owner.
.SH "RETURN"


* 0 on success.
* -EINVAL if \fIemitter\fP or \fIfile\fP is NULL, or the connections have
different hosts.
* A negative errno value on other failures.
